From: substrate
Subject: dix: NULL-guard SetFocusIn / SetFocusOut

DoFocusEvents -> CoreFocusEvents -> SetFocusOut can be reached with
a NULL DeviceIntPtr early in a client-connect sequence (matwm2
XGrabServer + XSelectInput on the root window) when the master
pointer's sprite has not yet been fully wired up.  The unconditional
`FocusWindows[dev->id] = NULL;` then dereferences NULL at offset
0x6c (the `id` field) and the server segfaults with signal 11.

Guard both helpers.  A NULL device simply has no focus state to
clear.

--- a/dix/enterleave.c
+++ b/dix/enterleave.c
@@ -190,6 +190,8 @@ EnterLeaveSetSubFocus(DeviceIntPtr dev, WindowPtr ancestor)
 void
 SetFocusIn(DeviceIntPtr dev, WindowPtr win)
 {
+    if (!dev)
+        return;
     FocusWindows[dev->id] = win;
 }

@@ -200,6 +202,11 @@ SetFocusIn(DeviceIntPtr dev, WindowPtr win)
 void
 SetFocusOut(DeviceIntPtr dev)
 {
+    /* matwm2's first XGrabServer / XSelectInput round can reach
+     * here via DoFocusEvents with a NULL device when no master
+     * pointer has been initialized for the active sprite. */
+    if (!dev)
+        return;
     FocusWindows[dev->id] = NULL;
 }

